SUMMARY:Southern Screen Film Festival with live Music by Sabine Mcalla
LOCATION:Blue Moon Saloon and Guest House\, 215 East Convent Street\, Lafay
 ette
DESCRIPTION:It’s night two of the Southern Screen Festival\, and we’re 
 celebrating with live music by Sabine McCalla ! A New Orleans favorite\, M
 cCalla brings soulful songwriting and a vibrant blend of American roots mu
 sic\, from Southern blues and soul to Brazilian samba. Her debut album\, D
 on’t Call Me Baby \, captures the sound that has delighted dancers and r
 evelers for years. Join filmmakers\, artists\, friends\, and fellow music 
 lovers for good company and soulful sounds. sabine-mccalla.com\n\n \n\nAb
 out the Artist\n\nSabine McCalla is a New Orleans singer-songwriter whose 
 music brings together Southern soul\, blues\, Brazilian samba\, and a broa
 d range of roots influences. Her debut full-length album\, Don’t Call Me
  Baby \, released in November 2025 and co-produced by Ajaï Combelic and S
 am Doores of the Deslondes\, has earned more than 1.75 million streams and
  praise from publications including No Depression\, Songlines\, and Uncut.
  She has shared stages with Nick Shoulders\, Rainbow Girls\, John Craigie\
 , and the Deslondes\, and performed at the UK’s End of the Road Festival
 . Her work also extends to film\, with an appearance alongside her sister 
 Leyla McCalla in Ryan Coogler’s Sinners and performance and music contri
 butions to Taylor McFadden’s Lovers . sabine-mccalla.com\n\nhttps://even
 ts.timely.fun/kw4jncf1/event/78509490/20261120200000
URL:https://events.timely.fun/kw4jncf1/event/78509490/20261120200000
